common: the MTP drafter stops at the draft length of the call

The defect

common_speculative_draft takes a draft length for each call (the n_max of
common_speculative_draft_params). The draft-simple drafter stops at that length. The MTP drafter
checks only the length of its configuration (params.n_max, 4 in the app). Thus each draft runs 4
passes of the MTP block, and common_speculative_draft then cuts the result to the length of the call
and discards the other tokens. The draft length policy of the app selects the length of each step
from the measured acceptance. In a chat turn of 51 steps on the phone it asked for 1 token 44 times,
and each of those steps ran 4 passes. One pass of the 4B Q8_0 on the NPU costs 17 to 21 ms with the
full head.

The change

The MTP drafter also stops when the draft holds the length of the call, with the condition of the
draft-simple drafter. A draft of n tokens runs n passes. Each pass reads only the passes before it,
thus the draft of n tokens is the first n tokens of the longer draft. The verify batch and the
accepted tokens stay the same.

The test

The scenario spec-limit of tests/fuzz/app (the tiny model with its MTP block) drafts with the limits
4, 3, 2 and 1 from the same position, and each pass writes one cell of the draft context. With the
change the drafts run 1, 2, 3 and 4 passes, and each draft is a prefix of the longest one. Without
the change a draft with the limit 1 runs 4 passes, and the scenario fails. The scenarios spec-parity,
spec-disable and spec-image pass. On the box CPU with the 4B Q8_0 (memprobe --turns --spec), each of
61 drafts ran the passes that it asked for.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Files:
    common/speculative.cpp

